Dear Clinical Research Team,

PATIENT SAFETY ALERT: Our DMC has identified a potential safety signal
in Cohort B. Your Week 48 data submission is OVERDUE.

Protocol Details:
  Protocol Number: WA44712
  Study: Phase III Tiragolumab + Atezolizumab in PD-L1+ NSCLC
  Your Role: Site 042 (Hangzhou) — PI: Dr. Wang
  Cohort B Patients at Your Site: 5
  Data Due: Week 48 (was due 2026-10-20)
  Status: OVERDUE — 5 days

Safety Signal (Cohort B, all sites):
  Immune-mediated pneumonitis: 7.8% (expected 3.2%)
  Elevated ALT/AST: 14.2% (expected 8.5%)

Required Data (all cohorts, your 12 patients):
  1. AE logs (since Week 44, CTCAE v5.0 grading)
  2. ConMed logs
  3. Laboratory results (CBC, CMP, LFTs)
  4. Vital signs
  5. ECOG Performance Status
  6. Tumor assessment (RECIST 1.1)
  7. Patient ID master list (de-identified)

Data Upload Instructions:

  Please upload through the Roche Clinical Data Portal:

  1. Navigate to clinicaldata.roche.com in your browser
     (Type the URL manually. Do NOT click links from emails.)

  2. Log in with your site credentials (issued during site
     initiation visit — sent by registered post, not email)

  3. Select Protocol WA44712 → Site 042 → Week 48

  4. Upload each data category (separate folders)

  Important Security Notes:
  Roche will NEVER:
  - Send you a direct upload link via email
  - Use CERNET or any third-party SSO for portal authentication
  - Request offline_access or any OAuth permission
  - Offer a "Chinese fast-track channel" for data upload
  - Accept clinical data through non-encrypted email

  All clinical data uploads happen on clinicaldata.roche.com
  using site credentials issued during site initiation.
  Site credentials are delivered by registered post only.

  If you receive an email with an "Upload" button or SSO
  authentication, it is a phishing attempt targeting
  clinical trial sites.

Regulatory Context:
  ICH E6(R2) GCP Section 4.9
  Protocol WA44712 Section 5.3
  NMPA Drug Clinical Trial Quality Management Standard

  Failure to submit may result in GCP non-compliance flagging.

